$ Synthetic run deck for the composite layup and ply results (tests/test_composites.py).
$ The ply results are synthesized by tests/op2_fixture.py (make_composite_op2) and
$ tests/h5_fixture.py (write_composite_h5).
$   CQUAD4 1  PCOMP 10   THETA 30 (material axis 30 deg from G1-G2)
$   CQUAD4 2  PCOMP 10   MCID 5 (its x axis is basic y)
$   CTRIA3 3  PCOMP 11   LAM=SYM: 2 plies given, 4 built
$   CQUAD4 4  PCOMPG 20  global plies 101 102 103
$   CQUAD4 5  PCOMPG 21  global plies 102 (here at the bottom) and 104 (SOUT=NO)
$   CQUAD4 6  PSHELL 1   no plies
$ Layup by hand (PLY_Z: the ply's mid-plane, from Z0 up):
$   PID 10: Z0 -0.025, T 0.04, FT HILL
$     ply 1  MID 2  T 0.01  0 deg  SOUT YES  z -0.020
$     ply 2  MID 2  T 0.02 45 deg  SOUT NO   z -0.005
$     ply 3  MID 1  T 0.01 90 deg  SOUT YES  z  0.010
$   PID 11: SYM, T 2 x 0.015 = 0.03, Z0 -T/2 = -0.015
$     ply 1  MID 2  T 0.005  0 deg  z -0.0125
$     ply 2  MID 2  T 0.010 60 deg  z -0.005
$     ply 3  MID 2  T 0.010 60 deg  z  0.005   (mirror of 2)
$     ply 4  MID 2  T 0.005  0 deg  z  0.0125  (mirror of 1)
$   PID 20: T 0.03, Z0 -0.015: 101 (0 deg, z -0.010), 102 (90 deg, z 0), 103 (0 deg, z 0.010)
$   PID 21: T 0.03, Z0 -0.015: 102 (MID 2, T 0.02, 90 deg, z -0.005), 104 (MID 1, T 0.01, -45 deg, NO, z 0.010)
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = nastran-pv composites
